{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n#include <map>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\nconst int mod = 1000000007;\nint n, cnt[1<<10], id[1<<10];\nint f[10][1<<10];\nvector<int> vec[10];\nmap<pair<int,ll>,int> mp;\n\nint power(int x, int e) {\n    int res = 1;\n    for (; e; e >>= 1, x = (ll)x * x % mod)\n        if (e & 1) res = (ll)res * x % mod;\n    return res;\n}\n\nint dfs(int x, ll state) {\n    if (state == 0) return 0;\n    if (x == n) return 1;\n    auto key = make_pair(x, state);\n    auto it = mp.find(key);\n    if (it != mp.end()) return it->second;\n    int ans = 0;\n    for (int mask = 1; mask < (1<<n); ++mask) {\n        ll nxt = 0;\n        for (int k = 0; k < (int)vec[x].size(); ++k) {\n            if (!(state & (1LL << k))) continue;\n            int cur = vec[x][k];\n            for (int bit = 0; bit < n; ++bit) {\n                if ((mask & (1 << bit)) && !(cur & (1 << bit)))\n                    nxt |= 1LL << id[cur | (1 << bit)];\n            }\n        }\n        ans = (ans + (ll)f[x][mask] * dfs(x+1, nxt)) % mod;\n    }\n    mp[key] = ans;\n    return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    int inv = power(100, mod-2);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        f[i][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int p;\n            scanf(\"%d\", &p);\n            int p1 = (ll)p * inv % mod;\n            int p0 = (mod + 1 - p1) % mod;\n            for (int k = 0; k < (1<<j); ++k) {\n                f[i][k | (1<<j)] = (ll)f[i][k] * p1 % mod;\n                f[i][k] = (ll)f[i][k] * p0 % mod;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i = 0; i < (1<<n); ++i)\n        cnt[i] = cnt[i>>1] + (i & 1);\n    for (int i = 0; i < (1<<n); ++i) {\n        vec[cnt[i]].push_back(i);\n        id[i] = (int)vec[cnt[i]].size() - 1;\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", dfs(0, 1));\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MOD = 1000000007;\n    static int n;\n    static int[] cnt = new int[1 << 10];\n    static int[] id = new int[1 << 10];\n    static int[][] f = new int[10][1 << 10];\n    static ArrayList<Integer>[] vec = new ArrayList[10];\n    static HashMap<Map.Entry<Integer, Long>, Integer> mp = new HashMap<>();\n\n    static int power(int x, int e) {\n        long res = 1;\n        long base = x % MOD;\n        while (e > 0) {\n            if ((e & 1) == 1) {\n                res = (res * base) % MOD;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % MOD;\n            e >>= 1;\n        }\n        return (int) res;\n    }\n\n    static int dfs(int x, long state) {\n        if (state == 0) return 0;\n        if (x == n) return 1;\n        Map.Entry<Integer, Long> key = new AbstractMap.SimpleEntry<>(x, state);\n        Integer cached = mp.get(key);\n        if (cached != null) return cached;\n\n        long ans = 0;\n        for (int mask = 1; mask < (1 << n); ++mask) {\n            long nxt = 0;\n            for (int k = 0; k < vec[x].size(); ++k) {\n                if ((state & (1L << k)) == 0) continue;\n                int cur = vec[x].get(k);\n                for (int bit = 0; bit < n; ++bit) {\n                    if ((mask & (1 << bit)) != 0 && (cur & (1 << bit)) == 0) {\n                        int newVal = cur | (1 << bit);\n                        nxt |= (1L << id[newVal]);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            ans = (ans + (long) f[x][mask] * dfs(x + 1, nxt)) % MOD;\n        }\n        mp.put(key, (int) ans);\n        return (int) ans;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        n = sc.nextInt();\n        int inv = power(100, MOD - 2);\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n            vec[i] = new ArrayList<>();\n        }\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            f[i][0] = 1;\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n                int p = sc.nextInt();\n                int p1 = (int) ((long) p * inv % MOD);\n                int p0 = (MOD + 1 - p1) % MOD;\n                for (int k = 0; k < (1 << j); ++k) {\n                    f[i][k | (1 << j)] = (int) ((long) f[i][k] * p1 % MOD);\n                    f[i][k] = (int) ((long) f[i][k] * p0 % MOD);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < (1 << n); ++i) {\n            cnt[i] = cnt[i >> 1] + (i & 1);\n        }\n        for (int i = 0; i < (1 << n); ++i) {\n            vec[cnt[i]].add(i);\n            id[i] = vec[cnt[i]].size() - 1;\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(dfs(0, 1L));\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.7881378e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -2.6344906e-05, -9.202534e-05, -4.7683704e-07, -0.0067215064, -0.38768762, -2.6106494e-05, -1.1920928e-07, -0.0116560375, -0.0005590545, -5.3404336e-05, -0.011966583, -0.0007338215, -0.00020346955, -0.02975111, -1.1920928e-07, -3.0994368e-06, -0.0040789987, -9.5367